<p>Early, partial results from Nepal’s parliamentary election point to a sharp swing away from long-dominant establishment parties, with the Rastriya Swatantra Party (RSP)—led by rapper-turned-politician and former Kathmandu mayor Balendra Shah—out in front. As of March 7, counting was still under way. The election is Nepal’s first since the youth-led, Gen Z-driven protests of 2025. Several outlets said the protests followed a social media ban, turned violent in places, and led to deaths before culminating in the fall or resignation of then–Prime Minister K.P. Sharma Oli. Analysts and outlets described the early RSP surge as a possible “tsunami,” fueled by frustration over unemployment, corruption, and decades of political instability that have weighed on Nepal’s largely agrarian economy. If the trend holds through final counting, Shah—35—could become Nepal’s youngest prime minister. Indian outlets said neighbors, including India, are watching closely, hoping for a steadier partner in a strategically important Himalayan nation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/880CEPDXLyOxn596_twDQJ6T6xfOQwxfEse-_2MSzW3LOfOsJMotka6A9MNukGwy0mYa76ZMPDivBLHXCdhYRK70Zo7MOEMUBsaR9T9f' alt='Supporters of different parties cheer as the vote count is underway, in Jhapa district.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Seat math: Figures from Nepal’s election commission cited in reporting showed RSP leading in 100 of the 137 seats at one stage. Counting continued for 165 directly elected lower-house seats, with the remaining seats allocated through proportional representation.</li><li>Establishment setback: Early returns cited by Reuters via Dawn showed the Communist Party of Nepal (UML) and the Nepali Congress each leading in about 10 seats, with Nepali Congress reported to have won just one at that time.</li><li>Country context: Reuters reporting cited by Dawn described Nepal as a nation of about 30 million, where decades of instability have weighed on an economy grappling with unemployment and corruption.</li><li>Why youth rallied: Profiles of Shah and the RSP link much of their Gen Z support to an anti-corruption message and a confrontational style, amplified by social media popularity.</li></ul><blockquote>At least one member from each household seems to have voted for it (RSP). Otherwise this type of tsunami would not have been possible, - Puranjan Acharya</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Nepali Congress leadership: Vice President Bishwa Prakash Sharma posted on X that the party accepted the voters’ verdict as results came in. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979312/ex-rapper-balendra-poised-to-become-nepals-premier'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>India (strategic view): Indian reporting said New Delhi is watching the outcome closely and hopes a stable government in Nepal can help advance India–Nepal development partnership efforts. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepal-election-2026-results-forerunner-balendra-shah-gen-z-protests/article70714599.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/how-nepals-gen-z-forced-a-government-collapse-and-is-now-dominating-election-kp-sharma-oli-balendra-shah-nepal-elections-11180445#publisher=newsstand'>How Nepal&#x27;s Gen Z Forced A Government Collapse And Is Now Dominating Election</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/rappers-political-party-leads-early-results-nepals-election-130850447'>Ex-rapper&#x27;s political party leads early results in Nepal&#x27;s first election since 2025 youth revolt</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepal-election-2026-results-forerunner-balendra-shah-gen-z-protests/article70714599.ece'>Former rapper Balendra Shah’s Rastriya Swatantra Party heading towards landslide victory in Nepal</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/explainers/nepal-election-results-balen-shah-prime-minister-gen-z-protests-13986781.html'>Who is Balen Shah, 35-year-old former rapper likely to be next Nepal PM?</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-early-vote-returns-suggest-massive-political-shift/a-76255769'>Nepal: Early vote returns suggest massive political shift</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1979312/ex-rapper-balendra-poised-to-become-nepals-premier'>Ex-rapper Balendra poised to become Nepal’s premier</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>